{"words": [{"text": "فَمَنۢ", "translation": "Then whoever"}, {"text": "بَدَّلَهُۥ", "translation": "changes it"}, {"text": "بَعْدَ مَا", "translation": "after what"}, {"text": "سَمِعَهُۥ", "translation": "he (has) heard [it]"}, {"text": "فَإِنَّمَآ", "translation": "so only"}, {"text": "إِثْمُهُۥ", "translation": "its sin"}, {"text": "عَلَى", "translation": "(would be) on"}, {"text": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translation": "those who"}, {"text": "يُبَدِّلُونَهُۥٓ ۚ", "translation": "alter it"}, {"text": "إِنَّ", "translation": "Indeed"}, {"text": "ٱللَّهَ", "translation": "Allah"}, {"text": "سَمِيعٌ", "translation": "(is) All-Hearing"}, {"text": "عَلِيمٌۭ", "translation": "All-Knowing"}], "sahih": "Then whoever alters it [i.e., the bequest] after he has heard it - the sin is only upon those who have altered it. Indeed, Allāh is Hearing and Knowing."}